 "answer": "**Step 1: Count numbers divisible by 5, 7, or 11 (union) up to 5000**\n\nUsing inclusion-exclusion:\n- \u230a5000/5\u230b = 1000\n- \u230a5000/7\u230b = 714\n- \u230a5000/11\u230b = 454\n- \u230a5000/35\u230b = 142\n- \u230a5000/55\u230b = 90\n- \u230a5000/77\u230b = 64\n- \u230a5000/385\u230b = 12\n\nUnion = 1000+714+454 \u2212 142\u221290\u221264 + 12 = **1884**\n\n**Step 2: Count those in the union that are also divisible by 13**\n\nApply inclusion-exclusion again, but with each modulus multiplied by 13:\n- \u230a5000/65\u230b = 76 (5\u00d713)\n- \u230a5000/91\u230b = 54 (7\u00d713)\n- \u230a5000/143\u230b = 34 (11\u00d713)\n- \u230a5000/455\u230b = 10 (5\u00d77\u00d713)\n- \u230a5000/715\u230b = 6 (5\u00d711\u00d713)\n- \u230a5000/1001\u230b = 4 (7\u00d711\u00d713)\n- \u230a5000/5005\u230b = 0 (5\u00d77\u00d711\u00d713)\n\nUnion\u2081\u2083 = 76+54+34 \u2212 10\u22126\u22124 + 0 = **144**\n\n**Step 3: Subtract**\n\nNumbers divisible by 5,7,or 11 but **not** by 13 = 1884 \u2212 144 = **1740**\n\nFINAL: 1740"
